### Core Rust API

These are the proposed exact interfaces. Struct internals described as private are not public construction shortcuts.

```rust
#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum Seat { Zero, One }

#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum ObserveErrorKind {
    Config, Shape, Dtype, NonContiguous, Aliased, State,
    IntegerRange, EnumRange, Sentinel, NonFinite, Engine,
}
#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct ObserveError {
    pub kind: ObserveErrorKind,
    pub env: Option<usize>,
    pub seat: Option<Seat>,
    pub field: String,
    pub detail: String,
}
// Implement Display + std::error::Error. Error paths may allocate strings.
// Display: "env=1 seat=0 market_int[WHEAT,0]: integer outside int64".

#[derive(Clone)]
pub struct ObservationGame { /* private Game + Arc<ObservationConfig> */ }
impl ObservationGame {
    pub fn from_seed(config: Config, seed_decimal: &str) -> Result<Self, ObserveError>;
    pub fn from_header(header: &TraceHeader) -> Result<Self, ObserveError>;
    pub fn game(&self) -> &Game;
    pub fn step_with_market_metrics(
        &mut self, actions: &[serde_json::Value],
    ) -> Result<kaggriculture_engine::StepMetrics, ObserveError>;
    pub fn prepare(&self) -> Result<PreparedObservation, ObserveError>;
}
pub struct ObservationConfig { /* private checked scalars + cost prefix */ }
impl ObservationConfig {
    pub fn new(config: &Config) -> Result<Self, ObserveError>;
}
pub struct PreparedObservation { /* private snapshot + shared validated config */ }

pub fn write_seat(
    observation: &PreparedObservation, seat: Seat, out: &mut ObsRowMut<'_>,
);
pub fn write_env(observation: &PreparedObservation, out: &mut ObsEnvMut<'_>);
pub fn encode_env(
    game: &ObservationGame, out: &mut ObsEnvMut<'_>,
) -> Result<(), ObserveError>;
pub fn check_row(out: &ObsRowMut<'_>) -> Result<(), ObserveError>;
```

`step_with_market_metrics` is only a typed forwarder to the public kernel for the later lifecycle; no auto-reset/reward/seed allocation lives here. Task 1.4 stages clones of `ObservationGame` for transactions. `from_header` owns the config from that same header; no `game_mut()` accessor permits replacing the engine behind the config. `prepare()` takes exactly one snapshot, validates both rows and all derived numbers. `encode_env()` calls prepare before any destination write. `write_seat`/`write_env` are infallible after preparation and do not allocate arrays; private constructors prevent forging unvalidated state. Tests assert a failed prepare leaves both destination rows unchanged.

Borrowed row fields (names match Python except nested `action_mask.can_act`→`can_act`):

